; SELinux policy module for the Linuxfabrik Monitoring Plugins.
;
; Written in CIL rather than as a .te file, so that `semodule --install` loads it as it
; is, on the monitored host itself: no checkmodule, no selinux-policy-devel and no
; module policy version that a newer build toolchain could raise beyond what an older
; host of the same major release reads. The module takes its name from the file name.
; Verified with policycoreutils 2.9 on Rocky 8 (enforcing), 3.6 on Rocky 9 and 3.10 on
; Rocky 10.


; Errors:
; * "Failed to start transient service unit: Connection reset by peer"
; * "Failed to get properties: Transport endpoint is not connected"
; Caused by (examples):
; * `systemctl --machine myuser@.host --user ... my.service` (`--user` is important here)
; Effects:
; * Allow D-Bus daemon IPC with unconfined services via FIFOs and UNIX sockets.
(typeattributeset cil_gen_require system_dbusd_t)
(typeattributeset cil_gen_require unconfined_service_t)
(allow system_dbusd_t unconfined_service_t (fifo_file (write)))
(allow system_dbusd_t unconfined_service_t (unix_stream_socket (read write)))


; The nagios types come from the distribution's nagios policy, which EL8 and EL9
; carry in `selinux-policy-targeted` while EL10 does not. An optional block is
; dropped when its required types are missing, instead of failing the whole
; module, so the same policy loads on every release. Where the nagios policy is
; present the rule applies, and it starts applying on its own once such a policy
; is added later. Where it is absent the plugins are labelled `lib_t`, which the
; base policy lets every domain execute and map anyway.
; Verified against selinux-policy 3.14.3 on Rocky 8, 38.1.75 on Rocky 9 and
; 42.1.18 on Rocky 10.
(optional linuxfabrik_monitoring_plugins_nagios
    (typeattributeset cil_gen_require chronyc_t)
    (typeattributeset cil_gen_require nagios_unconfined_plugin_exec_t)
    (allow chronyc_t nagios_unconfined_plugin_exec_t (file (execute map)))
)
